{
  "config_id": "apps",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Which applications this Studio bundle carries: the executable each ships, how it is presented in the selector, which installer component installs it, and whether it may register as the default document handler.",
  "audit_status": "verified",
  "_note": "One place, because the list was in five and three of them had already drifted -- launcher.py, epy_studio.spec (three sections), windows/epy_studio.iss (five sections), build.py and README, with the last two still saying 'three editors' after the fourth shipped. launcher.py reads this at run time and epy_studio.spec reads it at build time, so a fifth application is one entry here instead of nine edits. The .iss cannot read JSON; build.py refuses to build when the two disagree.",
  "apps": [
    {"id": "epy_reports", "display": "ePy Reports", "component": "reports", "register": "default", "description": "Technical reports — live preview, PDF / Word / HTML export"},
    {"id": "epy_slides", "display": "ePy Slides", "component": "slides", "register": "default", "description": "Presentation decks — reveal.js / PowerPoint export"},
    {"id": "epy_papers", "display": "ePy Papers", "component": "papers", "register": "default", "description": "Academic manuscripts — journal templates and citations"},
    {"id": "epy_craft", "display": "ePy Craft", "component": "craft", "register": "openwith", "description": "Batch LLM processing over your own reference library"}
  ],
  "_register_note": "'openwith' advertises an Open-with entry and never claims the default. ePy Craft consumes Markdown and text as batch INPUT and authors neither, so claiming the default would hand it documents it does not edit. That rule lived as a prose comment in the .iss, which is exactly what gets lost when a fifth application is added."
}
